@startuml
!theme plain
title Portfolio - planned project update happy path
skinparam shadowing false

actor "Portfolio owner" as Owner
box "Frontend design scope"
  boundary "Project studio" as View
  control "Interaction coordinator" as Interaction
  participant "API client" as Client
end box
box "External dependencies" #F0F0F0
  participant "Backend API" as Backend
  database "Database / file service" as Storage
end box

Owner -> View : edit project and select files
View -> Interaction : collect form and file changes
Interaction -> Interaction : track unsaved edits
Owner -> View : Save changes
View -> Interaction : submit editing intent
Interaction -> Interaction : validate frontend fields and file selection
Interaction -> View : show pending state and prevent duplicate submission
Interaction -> Client : submit project changes and selected files
Client -> Backend : planned project update request
Backend -> Backend : authorize owner and validate changes
Backend -> Storage : persist authorized changes (future connection)
Storage --> Backend : persistence confirmed
Backend --> Client : success and saved project result
Client --> Interaction : successful update
Interaction -> Interaction : replace displayed data and clear dirty flag
Interaction -> View : end pending state and show saved result
View --> Owner : show success feedback

note over View, Client
  Target behavior, not an implementation report.
  Happy path: validation, authorization and persistence succeed.
  Success requires a backend response.
  No browser persistence fallback will be used.
end note
@enduml
